add(WB,'Systems Development Workbook','Course workbook',['psychology','money-management','rule-based'], 'A scanned system-development workbook combining objectives, entry worksheets, exit design, expectancy and sizing. The false-breakout worksheet defines an entry and protective stop but leaves the profit exit incomplete. Its random-entry study specifies a 19-day exponential ATR and portfolio risk cap, so it must remain separate from the 1999 and 2009 book versions.', 'partial_rules','Van K. Tharp / Van Tharp Institute',None,[(wr,[[1,4]],'Workbook title and source copyright years 1996, 1997, 2002, 2003 and 2004 checked; a single publication edition is not established.'),(wr,[[60,60]],'Printed page 75: false-breakout worksheet with eight-tick stop entry, initial stop and day-one/day-two re-entry clause.'),(wr,[[66,68]],'Printed pages 83–85: 19-day exponential ATR × 3; ten futures markets without S&P; $100 including rollovers; 1% trade risk and 25% portfolio risk ceiling.'),(wr,[[75,75],[83,83]],'Printed pages 93 and 106 discuss stop design, intraday versus close-only stops, and partially specified exit filters.')],[('System objectives','Build a system around the trader’s constraints.'),('Entry worksheets','Treat patterns and trigger clauses separately from a complete system.'),('Exit and risk design','Combine protective exits, profit exits and portfolio risk controls explicitly.')],[falsebreak,random19], 'Scanned source read visually only on listed pages. Printed pagination jumps, so citations do not use a fixed PDF-to-printed offset. The scan’s completeness and exact edition are not established.')
