add(sid,'Stop Worrying Yourself Out of Profits','Article',['psychology'],'Explains how anxious expectations consume attention and alter interpretation of the same market event. It proposes reviewing the trigger/self-talk/feeling loop, keeping a worry diary and rehearsing alternative responses. The article says to change the thought and execution process rather than assume that swapping a trading system fixes poor execution.', 'reviewed_non_rule','Van K. Tharp',None,[(rid,[[1,5]],'All five article pages read; final source note identifies an excerpt from the second Peak Performance volume on controlling stress.')],[('Notice the trigger','Record the event, thought or feeling that starts worry.'),('Observe the feedback loop','Separate a market event from the trader’s interpretation.'),('Practice a response','Use the diary and mental rehearsal to improve process adherence.')],[], 'All five pages of this article were read. Its parent stress-control manual was not fully reviewed; the article supplies no deterministic OHLC strategy.')
