add(sid,'What Is a Trading System?','Article',['psychology','money-management'],'Explains that a trading system includes market selection, setups, entries, protective stops, re-entry, profit taking, position sizing and multiple systems. The reviewed sections connect these parts to objectives and a business plan. This is a specification framework: it helps reveal missing clauses but does not itself supply a fully fixed market algorithm.', 'reviewed_non_rule','Van K. Tharp; includes interview material with Ken Long',None,[(rid,[[1,9]],'Nine-page framework and source notes reviewed; market selection and system parts are described without a single complete fixed signal.')],[('Specify the whole system','An entry trigger alone does not define a strategy.'),('Check robustness','Evaluate fit, testing procedure and market selection.'),('Document missing clauses','List stops, profit exits, sizing and re-entry explicitly.')],[], 'Nine-page article reviewed, not the separate systems-development course it references. Conceptual system specifications do not equal a completed backtest.')
